<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bhim Singh II of Kotah</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1909–1991</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bhim Singh II was the last ruling Maharao of Kotah, a Hada <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chauhan">Chauhan</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajputs">Rajput</a> state in the Chambal valley of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajasthan">Rajasthan</a>, succeeding his father in 1940. In 1948 he took Kotah into the new Rajasthan union of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/princely-state">princely states</a> and became its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajpramukh">Rajpramukh</a>, or constitutional head, before the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharana">Maharana</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/udaipur">Udaipur</a> took that office when the union was enlarged later the same year.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bhim-singh-ii-of-kotah.jpg" alt="Bhim Singh II of Kotah" width="320" height="400" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bhim_Singh_II_Bahadur_Maharao_of_Kotah_1945-1947.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
